"ENSG00000153395","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0710631,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.500479,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"CUX2-","gene_id":"ENSG00000153395","module":"turquoise","kme":0.143096,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.787198,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Inhibitory","gene_id":"ENSG00000153395","module":"blue","kme":0.110931,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.851077,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false},"mathys2019":{"dataset_label":"Mathys et al. 2019","gene_ids":["ENSG00000153395"],"dataset_symbols":["LPCAT1"],"explorer":"explorer.html?dataset=mathys2019#gene/LPCAT1","cell_types":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_symbol":"LPCAT1","gene_symbol_current":"LPCAT1","gene_id":"ENSG00000153395","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.23835,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0263373,"nucleus_score":-1.34743,"pct_ad":0.187932,"pct_control":0.195964,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.990685,"donor_log2fc":-0.0310096,"donor_lfcse":0.0902378,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-3.93194e-06},{"cell_type":"In","gene_symbol":"LPCAT1","gene_symbol_current":"LPCAT1","gene_id":"ENSG00000153395","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.037999,"nucleus_log2fc":0.358918,"nucleus_score":3.24068,"pct_ad":0.131766,"pct_control":0.102397,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999889,"donor_log2fc":0.313829,"donor_lfcse":0.140906,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":1.56166e-05}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000153395","entrez_id":["79888"],"uniprot":["Q8NF37"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a member of the 1-acyl-sn-glycerol-3-phosphate acyltransferase family of proteins. The encoded enzyme plays a role in phospholipid metabolism, specifically in the conversion of lysophosphatidylcholine to phosphatidylcholine in the presence of acyl-CoA. This process is important in the synthesis of lung surfactant and platelet-activating factor (PAF). Elevated expression of this gene may contribute to the progression of oral squamous cell, prostate, breast, and other human cancers. [provided by RefSeq, Sep 2016].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8NF37","text":"Exhibits acyltransferase activity (PubMed:18156367, PubMed:21498505). Exhibits acetyltransferase activity (By similarity). Activity is calcium-independent (By similarity). Catalyzes the conversion of lysophosphatidylcholine (1-acyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine or LPC) into phosphatidylcholine (1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine or PC) (PubMed:18156367, PubMed:21498505). Catalyzes the conversion 1-acyl-sn-glycerol-3-phosphate (lysophosphatidic acid or LPA) into 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol-3-phosphate (phosphatidic acid or PA) by incorporating an acyl moiety at the sn-2 position of the glycerol backbone (By similarity). Displays a clear preference for saturated fatty acyl-CoAs, and 1-myristoyl or 1-palmitoyl LPC as acyl donors and acceptors, respectively (By similarity). Involved in platelet-activating factor (PAF) biosynthesis by catalyzing the conversion of the PAF precursor, 1-O-alkyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine (lyso-PAF) into 1-O-alkyl-2-acetyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine (PAF) (By similarity). May synthesize phosphatidylcholine in pulmonary surfactant, thereby playing a pivotal role in respiratory physiology (By similarity). Involved in the regulation of lipid droplet number and size (PubMed:25491198)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}